redfin 1095: voice proxy pacing (coder V3, 2026-11-14). Fixes 1090's robotic call audio.
- Cause: the DSP answers RT-proxy READ_V2/WRITE_V2 at once (~0.6 ms); 1090 re-sent on each answer -> ~1700 frames/s
  each way instead of 100. msm-pcm-afe-v2.c (mmap) paces with an hrtimer of one period, walking a multi-period buffer.
- kern.sweet_voice_proxy_pace 1 (default, next call): one read on 0x2000 + one write on 0x2001 per 10 ms (absolute mach
  deadline), 4 periods back to back per direction, a period reused only after its answer; downlink frame taken on the
  answer in issue order. 0 = 1090's data path unchanged.
- Call ring held at 30-60 ms (trim past 60 ms, -1 slip when min > 30 ms, +1 after underruns).
- Per-second "1s: PACED dl N periods ..." line (first 30 s, then every 10 s): periods, gap, busy/lost/late, dup/zero
  frames, rings, under/over/trim/slips, AFE LOW/HIGH_WM per port.
- kern.sweet_voice_proxy_gain_dl / _ul (dB, -24..+24, default 0, live).
- sweet_voice.c: CVP created on the proxy ports by default; kern.sweet_voice_proxy_opts 8 = 1090's switch after
  START_VOICE (1 wins over 8); opts mask 7 -> 15.
With kern.sweet_voice_proxy 0 nothing here runs (3adbc22 behaviour).

